  192 2ABC ~            ; result's significand -- shifted up a place when the leading one is at bit 126 rather than 127 --
  193 2ABC ~            ; and what comes off its bottom only a sticky bit (qst), ORed into bit 0, which is below the round
  194 2ABC ~            ; bit either way. Both significands have their lowest eleven bits zero (fifty-three bits at the
  195 2ABC ~            ; top of sixty-four): the multiplier's lowest byte would only shift a zero qr, so the loop starts
  196 2ABC ~            ; at its second, and the multiplicand's lowest byte adds nothing, so the addition starts at its
  197 2ABC ~            ; second. The eight-byte addition and shift are written out, not called: three times as fast.
