 2154 2ABC ~            ; after the shift, in the carry; the divisor's top byte in D and its low word negated in BC, so
 2155 2ABC ~            ; that taking it off is ADD HL,BC and SBC A,D on the carry turned round. A low word of zero would
 2156 2ABC ~            ; leave no carry, so then D is one less and the low word taken as 65536. The top bytes alike, the
 2157 2ABC ~            ; same ADD on a copy of HL tells the rest. The quotient's bits go in at the bottom of fpx,
 2158 2ABC ~            ; inverted, behind a 1 that comes out at the top when there are eight; each full byte is pushed.
