 3980 2ABC ~            ;
 3981 2ABC ~            ; which is one sixteen-by-sixteen multiplication with a thirty-two-bit result, the smaller low
 3982 2ABC ~            ; half the multiplier, and two with a sixteen-bit one -- a high half that is zero, as it is
 3983 2ABC ~            ; whenever a `long` holds an unsigned int's worth, dropping its term altogether, and one that is
 3984 2ABC ~            ; FFFFh, a negative int's, making it a subtraction. z88dk's runtime does the same (l_long_mult).
