 6698 2C44              ; the other -- C the low byte (0 for 256), B the high one and one more where C is not 0 -- which
 6699 2C44              ; the compiler works out (isel.c, select_block_move), and an odd count entered at the second
 6700 2C44              ; byte of the first pair. 31.5 T-states a byte for a copy, against 47 a byte for __x80_memcpy's
 6701 2C44              ; word counted down; 19.5 for a zeroing, against 38. __x80_mcpyp_* write A, BC, DE and HL;
